@baseUrl = http://localhost:8001/odata/v4/Service


### from original Fiori request:

POST {{baseUrl}}/$batch
content-type: multipart/mixed; boundary=batch_id-1779006529335-128
Accept: multipart/mixed

--batch_id-1779006529335-128
Content-Type:application/http
Content-Transfer-Encoding:binary

GET Orders?$count=true&$select=HasActiveEntity,HasDraftEntity,ID,IsActiveEntity,OrderDate,OrderName,TotalAmount&$expand=DraftAdministrativeData($select=DraftUUID,InProcessByUser)&$filter=(IsActiveEntity%20eq%20false%20or%20SiblingEntity/IsActiveEntity%20eq%20null)&$skip=0&$top=30 HTTP/1.1
Accept:application/json;odata.metadata=minimal;IEEE754Compatible=true
Accept-Language:de
Content-Type:application/json;charset=UTF-8;IEEE754Compatible=true


--batch_id-1779006529335-128--
Group ID: $auto.Workers



### OData $batch: Multiple GET requests in one batch
POST {{baseUrl}}/$batch
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=batch_read_001
Accept: application/json

--batch_read_001
Content-Type: application/http
Content-Transfer-Encoding: binary

GET Customers?$top=3 HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json

--batch_read_001
Content-Type: application/http
Content-Transfer-Encoding: binary

GET Orders?$top=3 HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json

--batch_read_001--


### OData $batch: Change set with create + patch (all-or-nothing)
POST {{baseUrl}}/$batch
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=batch_write_001
Accept: application/json

--batch_write_001
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=changeset_001

--changeset_001
Content-Type: application/http
Content-Transfer-Encoding: binary
Content-ID: 1

POST Contacts HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "Name": "Batch Created Test",
  "Description": "Created via $batch changeset"
}

--changeset_001
Content-Type: application/http
Content-Transfer-Encoding: binary
Content-ID: 2

PATCH /Contacts(00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001) HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "Description": "Updated via $batch changeset"
}

--changeset_001--
--batch_write_001--
